# Pull Request Administration Authority

The user has granted standing authority to review and administer DNR pull requests:

> Investigate and fix issues, merge suitable changes after required checks pass, and close obsolete or unsuitable PRs with an explanation. Maintain the dependency-update configuration to keep the queue manageable. Preserve branch protections. Deploy to production only when I request a deployment.

- Review the actual diff and relevant compatibility evidence before merging. Passing checks alone do not replace review.
- This authority includes preparing fixes on branches, committing and publishing those fixes, updating PRs, and posting explanations of review and closure decisions without separate approval for each PR.
- Keep the required checks, strict up-to-date protection, and existing review requirements. Do not bypass protections or force a merge.
- Keep related routine dependency updates grouped where appropriate; evaluate major upgrades separately.
- Report merged, fixed, closed, and remaining PRs with concrete reasons for unresolved items.
- PR maintenance does not authorize a production deployment. When the user requests one, follow the established [release workflow](../../docs/release-workflow.md) and the requested version-bump convention.
